## 11. Prospective check

The prescription top {{ V.v('config', 'prospective.top_k', 'int') }} and a baseline of the top {{ V.v('config', 'prospective.top_k', 'int') }} by pair proximity (`{{ V.v('config', 'prospective.baseline.feature') }}`) after the same redundancy filter were registered before any outcome existed (design §11.1, preregistration section 8). The comparison population is the {{ V.v('prospective_register', 'population', 'int') }} candidates passing the redundancy filter, and the two lists share {{ V.v('prospective_register', 'overlap_prescription_baseline', 'int') }} triads. The label window starts {{ V.v('config', 'prospective.buffer_years', 'int') }} year(s) after the data cutoff and lasts {{ V.v('config', 'prospective.label_years', 'int') }} years; the verdict date is {{ V.v('derived', 'prospective_verdict_date') }}. P1 asks whether the prescription top beats random ranking and P2 whether it beats the baseline in top precision; as in the lightweight validation, the lower bounds of both bootstraps must clear the threshold. The check script does not run before the verdict date and stops if an input file differs from its registered hash.

